File Index

/charDataStore.ts
Purpose: Caches the most recent character vitals/ancillary snapshot so useCharData can seed itself on a fresh mount (e.g. a live HUD theme switch) instead of starting blank.

/levelProgressStore.ts
Purpose: Tracks progress through the current level for the compact HUD's EXP gauge. Level comes from login_data (game:character-login, once per login; seeded from the window.__SA_EVENT_SNAPSHOTS__ snapshot for late subscribers) and is bumped by event:level-up; tnl (exp REMAINING) comes from every game:char-data. GMCP does not send the level's exp SPAN, so span = highest tnl seen since the last level-up and fill = 1 - tnl/span — logging in mid-level therefore starts the bar empty (server-sent span would fix it). A re-sent login_data for the same character+level does NOT reset progress. Module-level singleton that keeps listening with no subscribers, so a live theme switch/remount keeps the high-water mark. Hidden at MAX_LEVEL (51) or until level and tnl are both known. An exact exp-per-level announced by the level-progress plugin (shatteredarchive:exp-per-level, keyed by character name so arrival order vs login_data doesn't matter) wins over the high-water estimate, which remains the fallback. Also listens for shatteredarchive:score-sheet-exp (new 2026-09-26, world-time-and-identity.plugin.ts's `sc`/`score` scan) as a SECOND, independent way to learn name+level — confirmed live that game:character-login can be permanently missed for a character (a mid-session character switch while GMCP was disabled; login_data never re-fires even after GMCP is later re-enabled), which without this would leave the bar invisible forever (visible requires a known level). A name mismatch resets state exactly like a fresh login; a level change on the SAME name seeds tnl/span immediately from the reading's own xpToLevel rather than waiting for the next char_data tick; matching name+level is a no-op (publish() never re-runs, snapshot reference is stable).

/levelProgressStore.test.ts
Purpose: Pins the fill math, the hidden-at-51/unknown-level rules, span reset + level bump on level-up, login re-send vs. real relog handling, late-subscriber seeding, survival across unsubscribe, and snapshot stability (useSyncExternalStore). Separate describe block for the score-sheet-exp self-heal path, real example-character numbers (GameLog-DSL 2026-09-26): becomes visible from that event alone with no login_data ever, does not inherit a previous character's stale level/span, a level change learned this way seeds the new span immediately, a no-op when character+level already match (asserts snapshot reference equality), and a reading with no usable name/level is ignored.
